# Settings of the Loki + Grafana machine of the audit journal.
#   cp grafana.env.example .env
# and fill in every REQUIRED line. The file is read by docker compose. Keep it
# 600 and out of git (.gitignore covers it).

# =============================================================================
# Grafana - REQUIRED
# =============================================================================
# A Grafana account reads the journal of every account in the installation, so
# the stack refuses to start until this is set to a password of your own. The
# value is applied only when the grafana-data volume is created; the password
# of a running Grafana is changed with
#   docker exec pneumatic-grafana grafana cli admin reset-admin-password NEW
#   openssl rand -base64 24
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin

# Where Grafana listens. 127.0.0.1 means "this machine only": put a reverse
# proxy with TLS in front of it before opening it to a network.
# GRAFANA_BIND=127.0.0.1
# GRAFANA_PORT=3000

# The dashboard that opens on sign in. Any file of ./provisioning/dashboards/json
# will do; the default is the overview of the whole installation.
# GRAFANA_HOME_DASHBOARD=/etc/grafana/provisioning/dashboards/json/project-overview.json

# Alert rules for failed sign-ins, refused file downloads and a pipeline that
# stopped delivering are provisioned from ./provisioning/alerting/rules.yaml -
# thresholds are edited there, and Grafana re-reads the file on restart, not
# on a timer. They fire into the Grafana UI only until a contact point is
# added under Alerting -> Contact points.

# =============================================================================
# Loki
# =============================================================================
# Where Loki takes the records of the collector. Loki has no authentication:
# bind it to an interface only the application machine reaches (see the header
# of docker-compose.yml), never to 0.0.0.0 on a public host.
# LOKI_BIND=127.0.0.1
# LOKI_PORT=3100

# How long the journal is kept.
# LOGS_RETENTION_PERIOD=365d
